## Implementation Details

### 1. Backup Script Logic
The automation script performs the following core steps:
1. **Generates Database Dump**: Connects securely to `stapp01` via `ssh` and executes `mysqldump` against `kodekloud_db01`.
2. **Local Temporary Staging**: Transfers the `.sql` archive locally to the runner/jumphost.
3. **Storage Offload**: Copies the backup archive to the remote storage server `ststor01` at `/home/natasha/db_backups`.
4. **Cleanup**: Removes temporary staging files from the local filesystem.

```bash
#!/bin/bash
set -e

APP_HOST="stapp01"
APP_USER="tony"
APP_PASS="Ir0nM@n"

DB_NAME="kodekloud_db01"
DB_USER="kodekloud_roy"
DB_PASS="asdfgdsd"

BACKUP_FILE="db_$(date +%F).sql"

STORAGE_HOST="ststor01"
STORAGE_USER="natasha"
STORAGE_PASS="Bl@kW"
STORAGE_PATH="/home/natasha/db_backups"

echo "=== Generating database dump: $BACKUP_FILE ==="
sshpass -p "$APP_PASS" ssh -o StrictHostKeyChecking=no ${APP_USER}@${APP_HOST} \
  "mysqldump -u ${DB_USER} -p'${DB_PASS}' ${DB_NAME} > /tmp/${BACKUP_FILE}"

echo "=== Transferring to storage server ==="
sshpass -p "$APP_PASS" scp -o StrictHostKeyChecking=no ${APP_USER}@${APP_HOST}:/tmp/${BACKUP_FILE} /tmp/${BACKUP_FILE}

sshpass -p "$STORAGE_PASS" scp -o StrictHostKeyChecking=no /tmp/${BACKUP_FILE} ${STORAGE_USER}@${STORAGE_HOST}:${STORAGE_PATH}/${BACKUP_FILE}

echo "=== Cleaning up local temporary file ==="
rm -f /tmp/${BACKUP_FILE}

echo "Backup completed successfully!"
